# Commit message rules
- Always write commit messages in English
- Keep commit messages concise and descriptive
- Use conventional commit format when possible (feat:, fix:, docs:, etc.)
- Write in present tense ("Add feature" not "Added feature")
- Keep the first line under 50 characters
- Use imperative mood ("Add" not "Adds" or "Adding")

# Implementation / security
- Start from docs/map.md + docs/patterns.md + docs/testing.md; follow docs/ and .cursor/rules/
- Keep compiled docs in sync when behavior changes (map + the linked feature doc)
- Keep tests/Unit/Contract/SecurityContractTest.php green; add unit tests for new behavior
